$pages = [
    'what-is-aab' => ['The AAB platform','Scientific memory that remains understandable, challengeable and useful.','AAB helps countries preserve the reasoning around scientific work, not merely its final reports.','A country should never lose what its scientists learn.','Knowledge is often fragmented across institutions, projects, people and reporting cycles. AAB connects evidence, decisions, failures, contradictions, mechanisms and unresolved questions while protecting the authority of scientists and participating institutions.',[['Memory before certainty','AAB records what is known, why it is believed, what supports it, what challenges it and what remains unknown.'],['Reasoning with boundaries','The platform can organise evidence and expose relationships without silently turning possibility into scientific truth.'],['Country-owned participation','Countries can coordinate many trusted institutions inside defined authority, privacy and governance boundaries.'],['Human authority preserved','Scientists and authorised people remain responsible for review, approval and real-world decisions.']]],
    'how-aab-works' => ['The governed learning chain','From activity to evidence, from evidence to durable understanding.','AAB connects each step without erasing uncertainty or the people responsible for scientific judgement.','Every learning keeps its lineage.','Work begins inside an authorised country and institutional context. Evidence is collected, reviewed and connected to its source. Outcomes, failures and contradictions remain visible so later reasoning can be traced and challenged.',[['1. Define','Record the question, purpose, expected outcome, responsibilities and applicable governance before work begins.'],['2. Observe','Capture field reality, measurements, context and source material without silently rewriting prior records.'],['3. Review','Authorised scientists assess evidence quality, uncertainty, contradictions and whether an outcome is established.'],['4. Preserve','Store the reasoning chain so future teams can understand what happened, why and what still needs investigation.']]],
