    'countries' => ['National participation','One national workspace. Many trusted institutions. Clear authority.','Country participation begins with governance and an authorised relationship, not a generic account form.','A controlled country pathway.','An authorised representative first explores AAB and its responsibilities. Agreements, country data boundaries, official authority and nominated administrators are reviewed before a workspace is activated.',[['Explore and discuss','Decision-makers can request a private preview and assess fit before beginning a formal participation process.'],['Review responsibilities','Country agreements, governance obligations, permitted use and data boundaries are made explicit.'],['Nominate authority','Official country authority and administrators are verified and approved separately from account creation.'],['Configure and activate','The workspace remains in setup until required checks, institutions and governance controls are ready.']]],
    'institutions-researchers' => ['Institutions and researchers','Trusted participation is invitation-led and institution-bound.','Universities, research institutions, laboratories, regulators and approved partners participate as governed entities.','People do not forward profiles to create authority.','A country administrator invites an institution’s nominated official. Once verified and approved, its administrator can invite scientists and teams into defined roles, projects and workspaces.',[['Verified institution','The organisation is represented by a governed record with its type, country relationship, status and accountable officials.'],['Controlled invitations','Every invitation carries its country, institution, proposed role, inviter, scope and expiry.'],['Professional profiles','Qualifications and affiliations can be reviewed where a role requires professional or scientific trust.'],['Role-specific access','Administrators, scientists, field teams, reviewers and regulators receive only the access their responsibilities require.']]],
    'community-observations' => ['Community observation','A photograph can begin an investigation. It does not become a fact.','Public, farmer, student and teacher contributions enter a separate governed intake pathway.','Evidence candidate first.','A submission begins as a visual evidence candidate only. Consent, context, moderation and authorised scientific review determine whether it may support future evidence.',[['Email-verified contributor','Contributors verify their account by email. Phone numbers may be stored for contact, never as proof of identity.'],['Consent and context','The contributor confirms ownership, permitted use, relevant location privacy and requested context.'],['Governed moderation','Submissions may be accepted for review, quarantined or rejected without becoming scientific evidence.'],['Evidence eligibility','A separate authorised review is required before a contribution can support a scientific evidence pathway.']]],
    'governance-trust' => ['Governance and trust','Extremely intelligent. Never falsely certain.','AAB is designed to increase understanding while keeping evidence, uncertainty and authority visible.','Governance is part of the reasoning architecture.','AAB may identify contradictions, expose missing knowledge, connect mechanisms and support scientific reasoning. It does not silently convert a scenario into a fact, an AI output into human authority or an incomplete record into confidence.',[['Facts are not scenarios','Simulations, hypotheses and recommendations remain visibly distinct from validated observations and established outcomes.'],['No silent overwrite','Versions, reviews, acceptance records, changes and outcomes retain an auditable lineage.'],['Unknown remains unknown','Zero evidence is not confidence. Missing information becomes a named knowledge gap.'],['Authority is explicit','Accounts, roles and execution authority are separate. Scientists and authorised administrators retain responsibility.']]],
